## Why GPL

Aster v2's trajectory layer (Slice 10 onward) incorporates the Lambert problem solver from PyKEP (https://github.com/esa/pykep), which is licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later. The PyKEP Lambert solver is compiled to WebAssembly and embedded in the Aster v2 deployment bundle. Under GPL terms, this creates a derivative work, so the combined Aster v2 codebase distributes under GPL-2.0-or-later.

## What this means for you

If you use Aster v2's code or fork the repository:
- You may use, modify, and redistribute the code under GPL-2.0-or-later.
- Modifications you distribute must also be under GPL-2.0-or-later.
- You must preserve copyright notices and license information.
- You must make source code available alongside any binary distribution.

See NOTICE for attribution of third-party components.
